# File transfer over the network. SHIPPED DISABLED -- see
# docs/commands/tftpd.md, and telnetd beside this file for what this
# directory is and how to enable something in it.
#
# The same warning, slightly sharper: TFTP has no authentication either
# and this one WRITES. `-r /` serves the whole filesystem, which is what
# makes /bin updatable; narrow it if one directory is enough.
#
# `-1` answers from port 69 instead of a fresh port per transfer. That
# deviates from RFC 1350 and serializes transfers, and it is the default
# HERE because a stateful firewall on the other end drops the standard
# reply -- measured, not assumed. Drop it if the client's host has
# nf_conntrack_tftp loaded.
Name=tftpd
Description=File transfer over the network (TFTP, port 69)
Exec=/bin/tftpd
Args=-r / -1
Restart=always
Ready=notify
